## Routing Protocol

Routing is automatic when the VibeSOP Pi extension is installed. If the
current user prompt arrives with an extension injection — look for
`VibeSOP Routing Result` or `Matched skill:` — routing has already run
for this prompt: follow that result and do NOT re-run `vibe route`.

If no such injection is present on the current prompt (extension not
installed or no skill matched), run:

    vibe route "<user_request>"

then read `.pi/skills/<matched-skill>/SKILL.md` and follow its steps.

User-typed `/vibe-*` commands still go through `vibe route --slash`
(see Quick Commands). Human-invoked CLI discovery is unchanged.

For routing details, override protocol, and multi-intent handling: read `.pi/docs/routing-protocol.md`.

## Skills

Run `vibe skills list` to see available skills, or read `.pi/docs/skills.md`.

## Session Lifecycle

When the user signals session end, run `session-end`.

Signals: "that's all for now", "heading out", "收工", "再见", `/session-end`.

Details: read `.pi/docs/session-lifecycle.md`.

## Quick Commands

When the user types `/vibe-*`, run:

```bash
vibe route --slash "/vibe-help"
vibe route --slash "/vibe-list"
vibe route --slash "/vibe-install <pack>"
```

Full list: `vibe route --slash "/vibe-help"`.

## Pi-Specific Notes

- Use `read` to load skill files from `.pi/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md`
- Use existing Pi tools (read, write, edit, bash) for all operations
- The `vibe` CLI is available as a shell command
- Session management is handled by Pi; use Pi's `/new`, `/resume`, `/fork` commands
- Compaction is automatic — no manual memory flush needed

